<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Inner Mongolia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Inner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a> is the southern part of the Mongolian plateau, lying along the north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, now an autonomous region of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a>. Its grasslands were the home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donghu">Donghu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a> and Wuhuan and the base of states such as Dai. Under the Qing its Mongol banners were governed separately from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/outer-mongolia">Outer Mongolia</a>, and in the 1930s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> sponsored the Mengjiang regime there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/inner-mongolia.jpg" alt="Inner Mongolia" width="320" height="173" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ScareCriterion12 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%88%90%E5%90%89%E6%80%9D%E6%B1%97%E9%99%B52021.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
